# Copy this file to ".env" (in the same folder) and change the lines below.
# (The Start CleanCut file does this for you the first time.)

# 1. The folder with your movies. CleanCut can only see (and save to) this folder and the folders
#    inside it. Use forward slashes.
#    Windows example:  MEDIA_DIR=C:/Users/YourName/Movies
#    Linux example:    MEDIA_DIR=/home/yourname/Movies
MEDIA_DIR=C:/Users/YourName/Movies

# 2. Optional: a separate folder for the filtered movies. CleanCut can then save there too (and does
#    so by default); you can still pick another folder each time. Leave it out to save next to the movies.
# OUTPUT_DIR=C:/Users/YourName/Filtered Movies

# 3. Linux only: save files as your own user instead of root. Run "id" in a terminal to see your
#    numbers (uid=... gid=...). Leave these out on Windows.
# PUID=1000
# PGID=1000

# 4. Only if your computer has an NVIDIA graphics card: it makes CleanCut several times faster.
#    Without one, CleanCut uses the processor (slower, still works).
#    Windows: remove the # from these two lines.
# COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yml;docker-compose.gpu.yml
# COMPOSE_PATH_SEPARATOR=;
#    Linux (also needs the NVIDIA Container Toolkit): remove the # from this line instead.
# COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yml:docker-compose.gpu.yml
